    "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nWhen several stop_strs match within the same decode step, `_check_str_based_finish` records the first one in list order instead of the one that appears earliest in the output. `trim_matched_stop` then trims only that string, so an earlier stop string leaks into the response.\r\n\r\nExample: `stop_strs=[\"END\", \"STOP\"]` on output `\"... STOP ... END\"` records `matched=\"END\"` and leaves `\"STOP\"` in the text.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- Collect every matched stop string in `_check_str_based_finish` (`schedule_batch.py`) and record the one with the earliest occurrence in the decoded text (ties keep list order; single-match behavior unchanged).\r\n- This addresses the TODO in `DetokenizerManager.trim_matched_stop` about handling multiple matched stop strings.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nNew unit test `test/srt/test_multi_stop_str.py` (pure Python, CPU CI) covering single-match regression, earliest-match-wins under both list orders, no-match case, and `trim_matched_stop` end-to-end (trim and `no_stop_trim`).\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nNot applicable — O(small constant) per decode step on the CPU-side finish check, off the GPU critical path.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format code with pre-commit.\r\n- [x] Add unit tests.\r\n- [x] Review documentation requirements. No user-facing API or configuration changes.\r\n- [x] Provide correctness and performance results.\r\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37726078344](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37726078344)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37726078183](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37726078183)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37726078266](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37726078266)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
